    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="1013" n="1005" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg1005"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13121a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-11T11:00:00-04:00">July 11, 1941—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>386. We have received further information from a high authority of a foreign
                        government<anchor n="30" xml:id="d832-f1"/> to the effect that, according to
                    reliable and most confidential reports reaching his Government, Germany, Italy
                    and Japan several days ago entered into a secret agreement where-under Germany
                    and Italy recognized the special position in the Far East which Japan claims for
                    herself and in return Japan agreed to take action against French Indochina and
                    Thailand and later to attack the Soviet Union. A further such report from the
                    same source was to the effect that Japan’s moves southward and northward as
                    described above would be carried out simultaneously.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d832-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d832-f1" n="30" xml:id="d832-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram from Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek, <ref target="#pg1004">p.
                        1004</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d832-f2" n="31" xml:id="d832-f2-content">
                <p>See also memorandum by the Acting Secretary of State, July 10, <ref
                        target="#pg300">p. 300</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
